    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nEvery vim.diagnostic.set() call for a buffer that is not loaded registers a buffer-local `once=true BufRead` autocmd without deduplicating against the autocmd already pending for that buffer. Each pending autocmd closure also retains that call's diagnostics payload. If the buffer is never loaded, they accumulate for the lifetime of the session.\n\nAfter a long session with `rust-analyzer` on 0.12.4, I can get to 10s of thousands of pending autocmds and GBs of RAM used.\nApparently some improvements \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```lua\nlocal b = vim.fn.bufadd(vim.fn.tempname())\nlocal ns = vim.api.nvim_create_namespace('repro')\nprint('buffer loaded: ' .. tostring(vim.api.nvim_buf_is_loaded(b)))\nfor i = 1, 5 do\n  vim.diagnostic.set(ns, b, { { lnum = 0, col = 0, message = 'x' } })\n  local n = #vim.api.nvim_get_autocmds({ event = 'BufRead', buffer = b })\n  print(('after set() #%d: %d pending BufRead autocmds'):format(i, n))\nend\n```\n\nOutput on v0.13.0-dev-1017+gd36d05cbd5 (grows by 1 per call, unbounded):\n\n```\nbuffer loaded: false\nafter set() #1: 3 pending BufRead autocmds\nafter set() #2: 4 pending BufRead autocmds\nafter set() #3: 5 pending BufRead autocmds\nafter set() #4: 6 pending BufRead autocmds\nafter set() #5: 7 pending BufRead autocmds\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nRepeated `vim.diagnostic.set()` calls for an unloaded buffer keep at most one pending BufRead autocmd per diagnostic, so long-running sessions do not accumulate autocmds or retain superseded diagnostics payloads.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1017+gd36d05cbd5 (also reproduced on v0.12.4)\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora Linux 44\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1 + tmux\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\ntmux-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nHomebrew",
