        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think at this point it sounds like a win.\n\nBuffer-local autocmds are good if/when they avoid (1) having to maintain a parallel list of \"managed buffers\", and (2) \"lifecycle cleanup\" (the buffer disposes its own state automatically when it's deleted).\n\nBut I would guess that vim.diagnostic doesn't avoid either of those, and we now have 2 reported problems being caused by the current arrangement. So yes, a global autocmd is fine @nat-e , thanks both for looking into this.",
